{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 landing — rebased onto current origin/main (Gerrit 2360, patchset 6)\n\nTicket-state note: a prior session had already implemented Phase 2 (the approved option-(b)\nserve-degraded design) and pushed **Gerrit change 2360**, which reached LLM-Review +1 AND\nVerified +1. Rather than open a duplicate change, I landed the existing one. A plain Submit\n409'd on a Rebase-If-Necessary **merge conflict** in `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` (origin/main\nhad since added the startup-handshake subsystem — `select_probe_host` / `handshake_status` /\n`install_startup_handshake` + a `/health` `handshake` field — adjacent to this change's opcert\nadditions).\n\nResolved locally in a fresh worktree off current `origin/main` by cherry-picking the change\ncommit (same Change-Id → patchset 6, not a duplicate) and merging the two subsystems: kept all\nof origin/main's handshake functions AND the opcert guards, with a single `register_health_route`\nwhose `/health` now returns `{\"in_flight\", \"store\", \"handshake\", \"opcert\"}` and `run_mcp` wiring\nboth `install_startup_handshake` and `run_startup_opcert_check`/`_OPCERT_STATUS_ATTR`. Pure\nadd/add adjacency — no behaviour change to either subsystem.\n\nRe-verified after the rebase:\n- Held-out `tests/unit/test_opcert_public_counterpart_guard_879b.py`: 12 passed.\n- Regression sweep (mcp_health/opcert/handshake/trusted_env/health): 338 passed, 6 skipped.\n- Mutation proof (sandboxed): neuter the mint guard → AC1 mint tests RED; force\n  `opcert_signer_degraded` → False → AC3 degraded tests RED (5 RED total); restored → 12 GREEN.\n- Non-test diff 133 added lines (< 150 floor → no plan-review needed); lint + typecheck clean\n  via the pre-commit gate.\n\nPatchset 6 pushed; the prior LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1 were invalidated as expected and both\ngates are re-running. Will Submit once both are green again, then close\n`--class=incomplete-implementation --caused-by=d26a-8ffa-97cd-4b2a`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788021903553034658,"uuid":"2df0406e-fc6f-4483-8a4d-725958102978"}